126,"\\"" The New York City medical examiners office has recently identified a victim of the 9/11 attacks on the World Trade Center, Matthew Yarnell, who was 26 years old at the time of his death; his identity was confirmed through a DNA sample that was retested using a new technique. Forty percent of victims of the attack remain unidentified, but the medical examiners office remains committed to continued efforts to identify them.    

Explanation: 
M Matthew Yarnell's mother describes the experience of finding out her son who was missing for 13 years had been identified.  

The World Trade Center attack killed 2,753 people.

