164,"\\"" Prince Bishop, a long shot racehorse, won Dubai's Dubai World Cup, the world's richest horse race. Prince Bishop, ridden by jockey William Buick, stormed from behind to overtake race favorite California Chrome and win by four lengths. California Chrome, who ran a good race, took second place, a $2 million prize. 2. In 300 words or more, explain why the article calls Prince Bishop’s win a “shock victory” & explain why it’s not really a fluke. Read the article. Use specific terms defined in the course & details of the race to support your answer. Use mare & thorough in your answer. “S shock victory” can often be predicted by significant factors. Was this a fluke or not? At first glance, Prince Bishop’s win at Dubai’s Dubai World Cup may seem like a fluke or an unexpected & surprising win. After all, the racehorse, ridden by William Buick, trained by Dubai’s Crown Price, was a 14-1 long shot. It lagged behind the back of the pack for most of the race, gaining the most ground to make up,\\""",378718,3067.5191407618113,123.46068031573758,0.037914691943127965,0.8013651371002197,242.2966472459957,2769.0292062722147,0.0073115859459339525,47791,330928,0.7468863446918736,0.9709044004636865,0.6246599436434022,0.8707053661346436,0.9814453125,0.7531242370605469,0.005093595646321773,0.90283203125,0.004411783218383789,0.03149145878851414,0.912109375,0.02670785188674927,0.07989123985171319,0.92333984375,0.06586153954267501,0.6705261628488304,0.9709919088616319,0.6274156287610462,19194,35179,6.965184926342118,0.06521027950613029,0.03553418528009701,0.04300674889223146,2823.3818949805573,9.053635785456859,2.4898926747942065,10.86098589501236,6.088091803124744e-07,1.5158695184074954e-06,4.7491470219484163e-07,1.1824866381470082e-06,0.051926174663538105,0.07601437242701649,0.07917017377912997,25.712314011063427,19.43639003896387,28.355174992000673,30.12591182033065,17029,0
