347,"\\"" QPR manager Chris Ramsey defended Rio Ferdinand, a 36-year-old center back who has been struggling since joining the team, after he was criticized by fans for his performance in a recent defeat to Tottenham. Ramsey pra praised Ferdinand's effort and refused to blame him for the goals conceded. Ferdinand has not been playing at his best and some fans have been calling for his retirement, but Ramsey encourages him and acknowledges that mistakes happen when goals are conceded. 
In a recent football match, QPR's manager Chris Ramsey defended his player, Rio Ferdinand, a 36-year old center back who has been struggling since joining the team. Ferdinand has not been playing at his best, and during the match, he was responsible for both goals that his team conceded, prompting some fans to chant ""It's time to retire"" at him. Despite this, Ramsey pra praised Ferdinand's effort and refused to blame him for the goals. He acknowledges that mistakes happen when goals are conceded, and encourages Ferdinand to continue applying himself well in Training and in games. 












