418,"\\"" Qatar's national football team will train at the England FA's national football center, St George's Park, in May for their international matches against European opposition, despite the FA chairman Greg Dyke's criticism of Qatar hosting the 2022 World Cup. This is a commercial arrangement similar to other teams such as Barcelona and Galatasaray, and the income generated will be used for grassroots football. Northern Ireland, who will play a friendly against Qatar on May 31, have upcoming Euro 2016 qualifiers and will also face Wales in a friendly in Cardiff.\\""",378718,3067.5191407618113,123.46068031573758,0.09302325581395349,0.8091865181922913,242.2966472459957,2769.0292062722147,0.0073115859459339525,47791,330928,0.7468863446918736,0.9709044004636865,0.6246599436434022,0.8707053661346436,0.9814453125,0.7531242370605469,0.005093595646321773,0.90283203125,0.004411783218383789,0.03149145878851414,0.912109375,0.02670785188674927,0.07989123985171319,0.92333984375,0.06586153954267501,0.6705261628488304,0.9709919088616319,0.6274156287610462,19194,35179,6.965184926342118,0.06521027950613029,0.03553418528009701,0.04300674889223146,2823.3818949805573,9.053635785456859,2.4898926747942065,10.86098589501236,6.088091803124744e-07,1.5158695184074954e-06,4.7491470219484163e-07,1.1824866381470082e-06,0.051926174663538105,0.07601437242701649,0.07917017377912997,15.501637919340283,19.43639003896387,28.355174992000673,30.12591182033065,17029,0
