Would you prefer an American or Indian author for the classroom? Why?
Would you prefer an American or Indian author for the classroom? Why? For the purposes of a classroom setting, it would depend on the level of students and the purpose of the literature being studied. If the students are beginner ESL (English as a Second Language) students, an Indian author would be better suited. This is because their english is generally more simple and easy to understand, and the themes and subject matter is familiar to the students. On the other hand, an American author would be more suitable for higher level students, as the language is more complex and challenging, and the themes and subject matter is more diverse and universal. Additionally, American authors are often more well-known and well-studied, providing a  wealth of\\""",378718,3067.5191407618113,123.46068031573758,0.05128205128205128,0.799968957901001,242.2966472459957,2769.0292062722147,0.0073115859459339525,47791,330928,0.7468863446918736,0.9709044004636865,0.6246599436434022,0.8707053661346436,0.9814453125,0.7531242370605469,0.005093595646321773,0.90283203125,0.004411783218383789,0.03149145878851414,0.912109375,0.02670785188674927,0.07989123985171319,0.92333984375,0.06586153954267501,0.6705261628488304,0.9709919088616319,0.6274156287610462,19194,35179,6.965184926342118,0.06521027950613029,0.03553418528009701,0.04300674889223146,2823.3818949805573,9.053635785456859,2.4898926747942065,10.86098589501236,6.088091803124744e-07,1.5158695184074954e-06,4.7491470219484163e-07,1.1824866381470082e-06,0.051926174663538105,0.07601437242701649,0.07917017377912997,30.034725135192275,19.43639003896387,28.355174992000673,30.12591182033065,17029,0
