Article: The Mexican Grand Prix has been added to the 2014 Formula 1 calendar. The race, which has been absent from the F1 calendar since 1992, will take place in the Autodromo Hermanos Rodriguez, Mexico City, on March 12. Additionally, the event will be the third night race this year, following Malaysia and Singapore. There is an option for the race to renewed for the 2015 season. The Mexican Grand Prix has been added to the 2014 Formula 1 calendar, taking place on 12 March. The event will be the third night race of the season. There is option for renewal of the race for 2015. 
