716,"\\"" Chelsea striker Diego Costa said that he was close to leaving his previous club, Atletico Madrid, to join Liverpool in 2013, but he chose to stay with Atletico to continue developing as a player. Costa ended up signing with Chelsea in 2014, and he has since become the joint-top scorer in the Premier League. Costa has had some controversial moments in matches against Liverpool, including clashing with defender Martin Skrtel and being banned for three games for stamping on midfielder Emre Can.

Nevertheless, it's worth pointing out that later in the season, in a match against the same opponent, Liverpool, Costa's aggression and lack of control led him to be in a high-profile incident which led to a 3-match suspension.
This wasn't a isolated incident for Costa, who has always tended to have a high number of yellow and red cards, and this is a trend that has followed him in the seasons that followed.
