752,"\\"" Greg Dyke, the FA chairman, proposed increasing the minimum number of homegrown players in Premier League club squads from eight to 12 and redefining 'homegrown' as three years spent club before player's 18th birthday to improve the national team. Ritchie Humphreys, PFA chairman and member of the FA Commission, supports the proposals and believes they will make clubs think differently about recruitment and offer more game-time for homegrown players. The FA Commission aims to make the country's national side competitive at an elite level, and these proposals are part of that mission.\\""",378718,3067.5191407618113,123.46068031573758,0.09790209790209792,0.8135675191879272,242.2966472459957,2769.0292062722147,0.0073115859459339525,47791,330928,0.7468863446918736,0.9709044004636865,0.6246599436434022,0.8707053661346436,0.9814453125,0.7531242370605469,0.005093595646321773,0.90283203125,0.004411783218383789,0.03149145878851414,0.912109375,0.02670785188674927,0.07989123985171319,0.92333984375,0.06586153954267501,0.6705261628488304,0.9709919088616319,0.6274156287610462,19194,35179,6.965184926342118,0.06521027950613029,0.03553418528009701,0.04300674889223146,2823.3818949805573,9.053635785456859,2.4898926747942065,10.86098589501236,6.088091803124744e-07,1.5158695184074954e-06,4.7491470219484163e-07,1.1824866381470082e-06,0.051926174663538105,0.07601437242701649,0.07917017377912997,16.225490424316376,19.43639003896387,28.355174992000673,30.12591182033065,17029,0
