823,"\\"" Cheltenham have appointed former Yeovil manager Gary Johnson until the end of the season, task tasked with keeping them in the Football League. Johnson, who was at the club's recent matches, also joins forces with assistant Russell Milton, who has been in charge of 9 games since February. With performances improving, Johnson believes they can turn it around, despite being bottom of Sky Bet League Two. 2
 1. In a surprising move, Cheltenham has appointed former Yeovil manager, Gary Johnson, to guide them through the next season. 
2. As assistant, Johnson is joined by Russell Milton, who has been interim manager for the past 9 matches.
