824,"\\"" Former Vice President Walter Mondale, 87, was hospitalized with theflu at the Mayo Clinic in Rochester, Minnesota last weekend, but is now back home. He had cancelled an appearance at the Nobel Peace Prize Forum, where he was to introduce former President Jimmy Carter. His wife had passed away, after a long illness, on February 4, aged 83, and they had been married for 58 years.
It is good to hear the former Vice President of the United States Walter Mondale is doing well and back home after being hospitalized for the flu at the age of 87. In recent months, he has had a difficult time, including the loss of his wife, but it's positive news that he is recovering well. Let's hope that the former Vice President can continue to have a speedy recovery from this illness. He has been serving an important figure in American history. Mondale served under Jimmy Carter from 1977 to 1981. He also served as a U.S. senator representing Minnesota and as an ambassador for Japan.  Alongside his wife, they were married for 58 years before her passing\\""",378718,3067.5191407618113,123.46068031573758,0.08,0.8062947988510132,242.2966472459957,2769.0292062722147,0.0073115859459339525,47791,330928,0.7468863446918736,0.9709044004636865,0.6246599436434022,0.8707053661346436,0.9814453125,0.7531242370605469,0.005093595646321773,0.90283203125,0.004411783218383789,0.03149145878851414,0.912109375,0.02670785188674927,0.07989123985171319,0.92333984375,0.06586153954267501,0.6705261628488304,0.9709919088616319,0.6274156287610462,19194,35179,6.965184926342118,0.06521027950613029,0.03553418528009701,0.04300674889223146,2823.3818949805573,9.053635785456859,2.4898926747942065,10.86098589501236,6.088091803124744e-07,1.5158695184074954e-06,4.7491470219484163e-07,1.1824866381470082e-06,0.051926174663538105,0.07601437242701649,0.07917017377912997,21.949235483072698,19.43639003896387,28.355174992000673,30.12591182033065,17029,0
