1350,"\\"" To raise awareness of prostate cancer, Luton Town, a League Two football club, will rename their home stadium the Prostate cancer UK Stadium for one match, the club announced on Wednesay. The capacity of their 110-year-old Kenilworth Road ground represents the number of men who die of prostate cancer each year in Britain. It is the first time that stadium has been named after charity, and the club and the charity hope to reach out to more people through the vehicle of sport. 

 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
