1437,"\\"" Tony Pulis, manager of the West Bromwich Albion football team, believes that being selected to play for England's Under-2 striker Saido Berahino has been performing well despite missing out on a senior international call-up. )  Saido Berahino has been performing well for West Bromwich Albion, scoring 18 goals this season and four in his last seven games, but was overlooked for a senior call-up to England's squad.  Instead, Berahino was selected to play for Gareth Southgate's England Under-21s side against the Czech Republic and Germany at the end of month, which Tony Pulis, manager of West Brom, believes is a big honor itself.  Despite this disappointment, Pulis praised Berahino attitude and his mindset, stating that the selection is a significant honor.  Despite being disappointed, he praised Berahino's attitude and stated that selection to the Under-21 squad is a tremendous honor. 

 
 



 



 



 




 



 



