1609,"\\"" Barclays has announced its sponsorship deal with the Premier League will not renewal renewed when it expires at the end of the 2015 season, due to concerns regarding increased cost following a recent £5.1 billion TV rights deal. Barclays has sponsored the Premier League since 2001, and while the popularity of the league has increased significantly, the cost of promoting sponsorship through advertising and social media has also increased. The bank has used its sponsorship to promote itself globally, but will now reassess its priorities and prioritize UK retail and corporate divisions instead.\\""",378718,3067.5191407618113,123.46068031573758,0.1081081081081081,0.8122561573982239,242.2966472459957,2769.0292062722147,0.0073115859459339525,47791,330928,0.7468863446918736,0.9709044004636865,0.6246599436434022,0.8707053661346436,0.9814453125,0.7531242370605469,0.005093595646321773,0.90283203125,0.004411783218383789,0.03149145878851414,0.912109375,0.02670785188674927,0.07989123985171319,0.92333984375,0.06586153954267501,0.6705261628488304,0.9709919088616319,0.6274156287610462,19194,35179,6.965184926342118,0.06521027950613029,0.03553418528009701,0.04300674889223146,2823.3818949805573,9.053635785456859,2.4898926747942065,10.86098589501236,6.088091803124744e-07,1.5158695184074954e-06,4.7491470219484163e-07,1.1824866381470082e-06,0.051926174663538105,0.07601437242701649,0.07917017377912997,18.535735970828682,19.43639003896387,28.355174992000673,30.12591182033065,17029,0
