1828,"\\"" According to a Beverage Digest report, Americans bought less soda for the tenth consecutive year in 2014, with a 0.9% decline in overall volume compared to 2013, with Diet Coke performing worse than regular soda. Ccribed ba the continued growth of energy drinks and improved marketing by major soda companies. Despite the decline, the broader US beverage industry saw growth of 1.7% with increased sales of bottled water. 40 400 tons 400 tons 400 tons 400 tons tags, Summary The 10th 10th year of declining soda consumption in the US has been reported, with a 0.9% drop in overall volume. This decline is attributed to increased concern about the negative health effects of sugary drinks and the proliferation of alternative beverages, with diet sodas fare worse than their regular counterparts. The American Beverage Association is addressing the shift away from Diet soda by funding studies to showcase their benefits, while energy drinks and improved marketing have helped moderate the decline.
