1883,"\\"" The musical sea organ in Zadar, Croatia, is the first of its kind in the world, created in 2005 by architectural innovation and expert craftsmanship. It is a 70-meter long aerophone that contains 35 organ pipes built under the concrete, producing unique musical chords played through whistle openings on the quayside, activated by the movement of waves. This unique instrument has earned world recognition, including the European Prize for Urban Public Space, and provides a unique, ever changing musical experience for listeners lucky enough to visit the stunning coastline of Zadar.\\""",378718,3067.5191407618113,123.46068031573758,0.08955223880597013,0.8056042790412903,242.2966472459957,2769.0292062722147,0.0073115859459339525,47791,330928,0.7468863446918736,0.9709044004636865,0.6246599436434022,0.8707053661346436,0.9814453125,0.7531242370605469,0.005093595646321773,0.90283203125,0.004411783218383789,0.03149145878851414,0.912109375,0.02670785188674927,0.07989123985171319,0.92333984375,0.06586153954267501,0.6705261628488304,0.9709919088616319,0.6274156287610462,19194,35179,6.965184926342118,0.06521027950613029,0.03553418528009701,0.04300674889223146,2823.3818949805573,9.053635785456859,2.4898926747942065,10.86098589501236,6.088091803124744e-07,1.5158695184074954e-06,4.7491470219484163e-07,1.1824866381470082e-06,0.051926174663538105,0.07601437242701649,0.07917017377912997,15.244315552990884,19.43639003896387,28.355174992000673,30.12591182033065,17029,0
