1994,"\\"" Wu Jiayong, a Chinese construction worker, made a miniature kitchen in a Hong Kong airport terminal when he realized that he had no money to buy food, and used his rice cooker, which he had brought with him, and a power supply from an electricity socket in the Terminal to cook rice and cook other foods to remain nourished.Mr. Jiayong's improvised kitchen drew surprised and amused attention from other travelers, and airport officials promptly shut him down, but fellow travelers and airport vendors provided him with food and other necessities until he could board a flight home two days later at no expense. Mr. Jiayong had previously used the rice cooker during his month-long employment in Singapore, where he had been working to support his family.\\""",378718,3067.5191407618113,123.46068031573758,0.0790960451977401,0.8075798153877258,242.2966472459957,2769.0292062722147,0.0073115859459339525,47791,330928,0.7468863446918736,0.9709044004636865,0.6246599436434022,0.8707053661346436,0.9814453125,0.7531242370605469,0.005093595646321773,0.90283203125,0.004411783218383789,0.03149145878851414,0.912109375,0.02670785188674927,0.07989123985171319,0.92333984375,0.06586153954267501,0.6705261628488304,0.9709919088616319,0.6274156287610462,19194,35179,6.965184926342118,0.06521027950613029,0.03553418528009701,0.04300674889223146,2823.3818949805573,9.053635785456859,2.4898926747942065,10.86098589501236,6.088091803124744e-07,1.5158695184074954e-06,4.7491470219484163e-07,1.1824866381470082e-06,0.051926174663538105,0.07601437242701649,0.07917017377912997,17.640586537774652,19.43639003896387,28.355174992000673,30.12591182033065,17029,0
