2057,"\\"" Dozens of frozen goat carcasses were recently discovered at Connecticut's Butterfield farm. The farm's operators Tara Bryson and Michael Hearl are facing criminal charges for animal cruelty, after 70 dead animals were found on the property, and 74 sickly goats were seized by the state. The surviving goats are in rehabilitation facility in Niantic, awaiting adoption. 1
2
More than 70 dead animals have been found at Connecticut's Butterfield Farm, and dozens of frozen goat carcasses were recently discovered, prompting the arrest and prosecution of the farm's operators, Tara Bryson and Michael Hearl, for animal cruelty. The surviving animals are now kept in a state animal rehabilitation facility in Niantic, awaiting adoption. The discovery was made possible by the melting snow, revealing the scale of neglect and mistreatment of the animals at the farm. 



 

 



























