2136,"\\"" Apple will replace AT&T on the Dow Jones industrial average, a stock market index, because Apple's stock price has decreased following a stock split and is now eligible for inclusion.  This will take place after trading closes on March 19 and will be the first change to the Dow in a year and a half.  With Apple's entry, AT&T will leave the Dow Jones, and Verizon will represent the telecommunic sector instead.  Apple previously was not included in the Dow Jones because its stock price was too high and would have had a big influence on the index's average.  Two major criteria for inclusion in the Dow Jones are that individual stock prices should not give out too much influence on the average and also companies, must be influential in their respective sectors.\\""",378718,3067.5191407618113,123.46068031573758,0.1081081081081081,0.8074101209640503,242.2966472459957,2769.0292062722147,0.0073115859459339525,47791,330928,0.7468863446918736,0.9709044004636865,0.6246599436434022,0.8707053661346436,0.9814453125,0.7531242370605469,0.005093595646321773,0.90283203125,0.004411783218383789,0.03149145878851414,0.912109375,0.02670785188674927,0.07989123985171319,0.92333984375,0.06586153954267501,0.6705261628488304,0.9709919088616319,0.6274156287610462,19194,35179,6.965184926342118,0.06521027950613029,0.03553418528009701,0.04300674889223146,2823.3818949805573,9.053635785456859,2.4898926747942065,10.86098589501236,6.088091803124744e-07,1.5158695184074954e-06,4.7491470219484163e-07,1.1824866381470082e-06,0.051926174663538105,0.07601437242701649,0.07917017377912997,19.054518138058484,19.43639003896387,28.355174992000673,30.12591182033065,17029,0
